  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A calm workspace for a playful little companion.",
    "overview": "Pace brings the play; the workspace makes room for the task. Warm paper, brick red actions and the original cheetah artwork connect the desktop utility to its mascot without dressing up familiar controls.\n\nThe approved execution brief fixes the paper palette, orange/red character accents and quiet density. This is an operating interface: navigation, forms, transcripts, model downloads and explicit actions remain conventional. The signature interaction is the real sprite companion changing authored poses as it is petted, works and rests.\n\nThe first-run introduction has a bounded companion world: **Pace’s campsite**, the user's requested GBA-style pixel adventure. Forest framing, cream dialogue paper, Silkscreen lettering and the original campsite surround the unchanged Pace sprite. All `onboarding-*` tokens apply only to this introduction and its Settings replay; the workspace keeps its existing palette, platform typography and rounded controls.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm paper surfaces",
      "Quiet task-focused density",
      "Original pixel sprite actions",
      "Explicit, reviewable operations",
      "A pixel campsite for the first meeting"
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Campsite Boundary Rule",
        "body": "Apply the onboarding palette only inside the onboarding shell; workspace tokens retain their current roles.",
        "section": "colors"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep the original Pace artwork, colors and authored pose timing intact.",
      "Do use real native state and explain unavailable desktop capabilities.",
      "Do keep generated text reviewable before applying or running it.",
      "Do keep navigation and form controls familiar and keyboard accessible.",
      "Do keep the campsite palette, Silkscreen lettering and square frames scoped to onboarding and its replay.",
      "Do preserve readable sans explanations, optional setup and reduced-motion behavior in the campsite."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't fabricate assistant replies, transcripts, download completion or capture success.",
      "Don't imply macOS screen-capture exclusion; expose quick hide clearly.",
      "Don't add decorative texture, fonts or repetitive dashboard tiles to the workspace."
    ]
  }
}
